course: dictionary
lesson: 6506
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word needle is a good example. «A puppy's needle-sharp baby teeth fall out at about four to six months.» Here needle-sharp means very sharp, like the point of a needle.
explain: «A magnetised needle on a leaf floating in water turns to point north.» This needle is not for sewing. It is a thin pointer on a compass, and the clue is that it points north. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence best, then test it by putting that meaning into the sentence.
explain: Needles also appear in health and sewing. In «The rules that seem odd have good reasons: no food beforehand so nothing can come up into the lungs, numbing cream so the needle hurts less», the needle is the thin part used for an injection, and the cream is the clue that makes it hurt less.
fact: A needle is a very thin, sharp piece of metal with a hole, called the eye, for thread.
fact: Pine needles are the thin, pointed leaves of pine and other evergreen trees.
fact: A compass needle is a thin pointer that turns to point to magnetic north.
fact: In a doctor's or nurse's syringe, the needle is the thin hollow part used for injections, such as vaccinations.
fact: Never pick up a needle you find on the ground, in a park or on a beach. Tell an adult, because used needles can carry germs.
exercise: «A magnetised needle on a leaf floating in water turns to point north.» In this sentence, what does the needle do? | *It points north | It gives a jab | It falls off the leaf | It sews a button
exercise: «A puppy's needle-sharp baby teeth fall out at about four to six months.» Find and copy the word that tells you the teeth are very sharp. | baby | *needle-sharp | months | puppy's
exercise: A child finds a needle on the beach. What should the child do? | Put it in a pocket | Use it to sew a bag | Pick it up and take it home | *Tell an adult and do not touch it
test:
Pine needles are the thin, pointed leaves of pine and other evergreen trees. What are pine needles? | *Thin, pointed leaves | Sharp metal tools for sewing | Hollow parts of a syringe | Long sticks used for knitting
«Knitting needles are long sticks for knitting.» In this sentence, what are knitting needles used for? | Sewing buttons on a coat | Giving injections | *Knitting | Pointing north on a compass
exam: The phrase «a needle in a haystack» means something that is hard to find, so what does it mean when someone says it? | Made of metal and very sharp | A short, thin pointer on a dial | Very easy to find | *Very hard to find
